Description:

Admins can manage global Sieve scripts over ManageSieve again, both
server-wide and per domain, and attach them to shared mailboxes.  Previously
an admin's ManageSieve session failed, because Cyrus tried to store the
scripts in a #sieve mailbox under the admin's nonexistent INBOX.  Global
scripts are now stored in a shared #sieve mailbox (one per domain) with an
empty ACL.


Documentation:

docsrc/reference/admin/sieve.rst


Config changes:

None.


Upgrade instructions:

Global scripts installed directly in the global Sieve directory keep working.
The first time an admin connects to timsieved, they are moved into the shared
#sieve mailbox, and from then on should be managed over ManageSieve.


